{"key":"enterprise/T1555.002","id":"T1555.002","name":"Securityd Memory","domain":"enterprise","level":"subtechnique","parent_id":"T1555","tactics":["credential-access"],"platforms":["Linux","macOS"],"environments":["cloud-hosted-endpoint","onprem"],"environment_basis":"project_taxonomy_from_upstream_platforms","summary":"An adversary with root access may gather credentials by reading `securityd`’s memory. `securityd` is a service/daemon responsible for implementing security protocols such as encryption and authorization. A privileged adversary may be able to scan through `securityd`'s memory to find the correct sequence of keys to decrypt the user’s logon keychain. This may provide the adversary with various plaintext passwords, such as those for users, WiFi,…","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1555/002","source_stix_id":"attack-pattern--1a80d097-54df-41d8-9d33-34e755ec5e72","source_modified":"2025-10-24T17:48:28.055Z","source_object_version":"1.2","telemetry":{"status":"mapped","components":[{"id":"DC0064","name":"Command Execution","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0064","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--685f917a-e95e-4ba0-ade1-c7d354dae6e0","page":"telemetry/DC0064/"},{"id":"DC0055","name":"File Access","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0055","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--235b7491-2d2b-4617-9a52-3c0783680f71","page":"telemetry/DC0055/"},{"id":"DC0035","name":"Process Access","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0035","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--1887a270-576a-4049-84de-ef746b2572d6","page":"telemetry/DC0035/"},{"id":"DC0032","name":"Process Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0032","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--3d20385b-24ef-40e1-9f56-f39750379077","page":"telemetry/DC0032/"}],"strategies":[{"id":"DET0057","name":"Detect Suspicious Access to securityd Memory for Credential Extraction","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0057","stix_id":"x-mitre-d